# Implementation Plan — WhatsApp Customer Support Bot Integration

This plan details the design and implementation steps for integrating a production-ready WhatsApp Customer Support Bot into the Sparky backend using the official Meta WhatsApp Cloud API.

## Goal Description

Integrate a Meta WhatsApp Business Cloud API webhook, message parser, conversation manager, state-machine-based chatbot (with booking lookup, service listings, FAQs, support ticket flow, human-agent handoff, and modular AI fallback), and secure admin APIs for support agents to manage conversations and tickets. All existing code must remain functional and intact.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Phone Number Format**: The existing database uses 10-digit Indian numbers (`/^[6-9]\d{9}$/`). Incoming WhatsApp messages from Meta always include international prefixes (e.g., `91` for India). We will automatically normalize phone numbers by stripping country codes (like `91` or `+91`) and non-digit characters to ensure 10-digit compatibility.
> - **Support Ticket Auto-generation**: The existing `SupportTicket` model has `ticketNumber` and `slaDeadline` marked as required, but the existing API creation route `/api/support/tickets` does not provide them. We will add a pre-save hook to the `SupportTicket` model to auto-generate a ticket number (format `TKT + YYMMDD + 4-digit sequence`) and set a 24-hour default SLA deadline. This prevents validation errors globally.

